<ontology/use_metallurgy_tinplate/use_metallurgy_tinplate__0484__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. BRASS" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Zinc Crude in Cakes used in Metallurgy, Smelting, Brass & Tinplate: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. BRASS"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "The zinc reduced to the metallic state by the agency of the charcoal, combined with the copper, into an alloy which formed, on cooling, a lump at the bottom of the crucible."@en ;
